/// Status: The `Status` type defines a logical error model that is suitable for different programming environments, including REST APIs and RPC APIs. It is used by [gRPC](https://github.com/grpc). Each `Status` message contains three pieces of data: error code, error message, and error details. You can find out more about this error model and how to work with it in the [API Design Guide](https://cloud.google.com/apis/design/errors).
pub struct Status {
  /// The status code, which should be an enum value of google.rpc.Code.
  pub code as "code,omitempty": Int = 0
  /// A list of messages that carry the error details. There is a common set of message types for APIs to use.
  pub details as "details,omitempty": List[json.Value] = []
  /// A developer-facing error message, which should be in English. Any user-facing error message should be localized and sent in the google.rpc.Status.details field, or localized by the client.
  pub message as "message,omitempty": Str = ""
} derive Json

/// Step: Defines a particular step within a Cloud Dataflow job. A job consists of multiple steps, each of which performs some specific operation as part of the overall job. Data is typically passed from one step to another as part of the job. **Note:** The properties of this object are not stable and might change. Here's an example of a sequence of steps which together implement a Map-Reduce job: * Read a collection of data from some source, parsing the collection's elements. * Validate the elements. * Apply a user-defined function to map each element to some value and extract an element-specific key value. * Group elements with the same key into a single element with that key, transforming a multiply-keyed collection into a uniquely-keyed collection. * Write the elements out to some data sink. Note that the Cloud Dataflow service may be used to run many different types of jobs, not just Map-Reduce.
pub struct Step {
  /// The kind of step in the Cloud Dataflow job.
  pub kind as "kind,omitempty": Str = ""
  /// The name that identifies the step. This must be unique for each step with respect to all other steps in the Cloud Dataflow job.
  pub name as "name,omitempty": Str = ""
  /// Named properties associated with the step. Each kind of predefined step has its own required set of properties. Must be provided on Create. Only retrieved with JOB_VIEW_ALL.
  pub properties as "properties,omitempty": json.Value? = None
} derive Json

